# Reuse Rules (Audit)

```yaml
rules:

  - id: RULE_01
    name: FAN_BEFORE_CODE
    description: >
      Before creating any artifact, check FAN Registry.
      Feature must have FAN identity before implementation.
    enforcement: PRE_COMMIT

  - id: RULE_02
    name: ASI_BEFORE_IMPLEMENTATION
    description: >
      ASI must declare integration path before code.
      Assembly System Integration is mandatory.
    enforcement: PRE_COMMIT

  - id: RULE_03
    name: HOOKPOINT_BEFORE_EXTENSION
    description: >
      Hookpoint must be defined before extending.
      Authority boundary must be declared.
    enforcement: PRE_COMMIT

  - id: RULE_04
    name: REUSE_BEFORE_REIMPLEMENT
    description: >
      MUST reuse existing implementation before reimplement.
      Check hacedle, fem, and FAN Registry first.
    enforcement: CSA_AUDIT_PASS
    violation:
      severity: FAIL
      action: DELETE_AND_REEXPORT

  - id: RULE_05
    name: AUTHORITY_BEFORE_CAPABILITY
    description: >
      Authority must be established before capability use.
      Check ownership rules.
    enforcement: BUILD_TIME

  - id: RULE_06
    name: CERTIFICATION_REQUIRES_INDEPENDENT_EXECUTION
    description: >
      Artifact MUST be tested by CSA-owned scripts,
      not by builder's own test harness.
    enforcement: POST_BUILD
    violation:
      severity: FAIL
      action: REJECT_CERTIFICATION

reuse_checklist:

  before_creating:
    - Check FAN Registry for existing feature
    - Check hacedle for existing implementation
    - Check ASI for integration path
    - Check Hookpoint for authority boundary

  audit_targets:
    - brain/master/provider/gguf/*
    - brain/master/src/tokenizer/*
    - brain/master/src/runtime/*
    - brain/master/src/inference/*
```